1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,242
A ball tossed to a friend.

2
00:00:02,242 --> 00:00:03,546
Water from a hose.

3
00:00:03,546 --> 00:00:05,292
A long jumper in the air.

4
00:00:05,692 --> 00:00:08,108
All three curve in the very same way.

5
00:00:08,108 --> 00:00:09,213
Why that shape?

6
00:00:09,663 --> 00:00:11,861
Aarav tests it on his study table.

7
00:00:11,861 --> 00:00:16,128
He flicks one coin off the edge, and
lets another coin fall at the same

8
00:00:16,128 --> 00:00:17,028
moment.

9
00:00:17,090 --> 00:00:18,864
The flicked coin flies far.

10
00:00:18,864 --> 00:00:20,777
The other drops straight down.

11
00:00:20,777 --> 00:00:22,793
Which one hits the floor first?

12
00:00:23,293 --> 00:00:25,452
Most people say the dropped coin.

13
00:00:25,452 --> 00:00:27,860
Let's find out, and see exactly why.

14
00:00:28,510 --> 00:00:30,122
So what is a projectile?

15
00:00:30,472 --> 00:00:34,577
It is any object that is thrown,
and then moves only under gravity.

16
00:00:34,977 --> 00:00:38,263
A thrown ball, a long
jumper, a catapult stone.

17
00:00:38,263 --> 00:00:41,087
Once released, only gravity pulls on them.

18
00:00:41,487 --> 00:00:44,789
A rocket with its engine
on is not a projectile.

19
00:00:44,789 --> 00:00:46,506
The engine still pushes.

20
00:00:46,506 --> 00:00:48,590
We also ignore air resistance.

21
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:51,473
Aarav's test on the motion notebook.

22
00:00:51,473 --> 00:00:53,944
Two balls, same height, same moment.

23
00:00:54,294 --> 00:00:56,248
The dark ball is just dropped.

24
00:00:56,248 --> 00:00:59,823
The blue ball is pushed sideways
at five metres per second.

25
00:01:00,223 --> 00:01:01,451
Watch the heights.

26
00:01:01,451 --> 00:01:04,590
At every flash, both balls
are at the same level.

27
00:01:04,990 --> 00:01:07,189
They land together, after one second.

28
00:01:07,189 --> 00:01:09,757
The height graph for
both is the same curve.

29
00:01:10,157 --> 00:01:11,302
Slow-mo replay.

30
00:01:11,302 --> 00:01:13,709
Freeze, and draw the velocities.

31
00:01:14,059 --> 00:01:16,643
Sideways, the blue arrow never changes.

32
00:01:16,643 --> 00:01:19,139
Five metres per second, all the way.

33
00:01:19,539 --> 00:01:23,994
Downwards, the violet arrow grows by
nine point eight metres per second,

34
00:01:23,994 --> 00:01:24,989
every second.

35
00:01:24,989 --> 00:01:26,988
Exactly like the dropped ball.

36
00:01:27,638 --> 00:01:28,538
Your turn.

37
00:01:28,452 --> 00:01:30,856
Push the blue ball three times faster.

38
00:01:30,856 --> 00:01:34,084
Does it land sooner,
later, or at the same time?

39
00:01:34,084 --> 00:01:35,282
Pause and decide.

40
00:01:38,482 --> 00:01:39,622
The same time!

41
00:01:39,622 --> 00:01:42,942
A faster push sends it
farther, not faster down.

42
00:01:42,942 --> 00:01:45,223
Fall time depends only on height.

43
00:01:45,873 --> 00:01:48,857
Now let's throw at an
angle, like a real throw.

44
00:01:49,207 --> 00:01:53,285
Speed twenty metres per second, at
thirty degrees above the ground.

45
00:01:53,685 --> 00:01:55,955
Split the throw into two parts.

46
00:01:55,955 --> 00:01:57,626
Across, u cos theta.

47
00:01:57,626 --> 00:01:59,086
Up, u sin theta.

48
00:01:59,486 --> 00:02:03,199
Across, that is about seventeen
point three metres per second.

49
00:02:03,199 --> 00:02:04,382
Up, it is ten.

50
00:02:04,782 --> 00:02:05,731
Let it fly.

51
00:02:05,731 --> 00:02:07,870
The across speed stays the same.

52
00:02:07,870 --> 00:02:11,908
The up speed shrinks to zero at
the top, then grows downwards.

53
00:02:12,308 --> 00:02:15,512
And gravity, the red arrow,
points down the whole time.

54
00:02:15,512 --> 00:02:18,126
At the start, at the top, and at the end.

55
00:02:18,776 --> 00:02:21,128
Now the rules, one step at a time.

56
00:02:21,478 --> 00:02:22,420
Step one.

57
00:02:22,420 --> 00:02:24,418
Split the start velocity.

58
00:02:24,418 --> 00:02:26,439
u x equals u cos theta.

59
00:02:26,439 --> 00:02:28,460
u y equals u sin theta.

60
00:02:29,210 --> 00:02:30,123
Step two.

61
00:02:30,123 --> 00:02:32,683
Across, there is no acceleration.

62
00:02:32,683 --> 00:02:35,444
So x equals u cos theta, times t.

63
00:02:36,194 --> 00:02:37,210
Step three.

64
00:02:37,210 --> 00:02:40,779
Up and down, the
acceleration is g, downwards.

65
00:02:40,779 --> 00:02:44,724
So y equals u sin theta
t, minus half g t squared.

66
00:02:45,474 --> 00:02:46,510
Step four.

67
00:02:46,510 --> 00:02:48,152
The velocity parts.

68
00:02:48,152 --> 00:02:50,188
v x stays u cos theta.

69
00:02:50,188 --> 00:02:53,403
And v y equals u sin theta minus g t.

70
00:02:54,153 --> 00:02:55,221
Remember this.

71
00:02:55,221 --> 00:02:56,959
One throw, two motions.

72
00:02:56,959 --> 00:02:59,575
Steady across, free fall up and down.

73
00:03:00,275 --> 00:03:01,412
Side by side.

74
00:03:01,412 --> 00:03:05,148
Across, the ball moves like
a car on cruise control.

75
00:03:05,148 --> 00:03:06,716
Same gap every tick.

76
00:03:07,116 --> 00:03:10,377
Up and down, it moves like
a ball thrown straight up.

77
00:03:10,377 --> 00:03:12,524
It slows, stops, and falls back.

78
00:03:13,124 --> 00:03:14,141
Now you try.

79
00:03:14,141 --> 00:03:18,228
At the very top of the path,
is the speed of the ball zero?

80
00:03:18,228 --> 00:03:19,492
Pause and decide.

81
00:03:22,692 --> 00:03:23,592
No!

82
00:03:23,176 --> 00:03:25,731
Only the up and down part is zero.

83
00:03:25,731 --> 00:03:28,644
The across part, u cos theta, remains.

84
00:03:28,644 --> 00:03:31,094
So the top speed is u cos theta.

85
00:03:31,744 --> 00:03:33,479
Now, one worked example.

86
00:03:33,829 --> 00:03:38,250
A ball is thrown at twenty metres
per second, at thirty degrees.

87
00:03:38,250 --> 00:03:42,080
Find its position and velocity
at one point five seconds.

88
00:03:42,580 --> 00:03:43,480
Across.

89
00:03:43,274 --> 00:03:46,839
x equals seventeen point
three times one point five.

90
00:03:46,839 --> 00:03:48,616
About twenty six metres.

91
00:03:49,366 --> 00:03:50,266
Up.

92
00:03:49,872 --> 00:03:55,477
y equals ten times one point five, minus
half g times one point five squared.

93
00:03:55,477 --> 00:03:56,939
About four metres.

94
00:03:57,689 --> 00:03:58,589
Velocity.

95
00:03:58,534 --> 00:04:00,992
v x stays seventeen point three.

96
00:04:00,992 --> 00:04:06,163
v y is ten minus nine point eight
times one point five, minus four point

97
00:04:06,163 --> 00:04:07,063
seven.

98
00:04:06,842 --> 00:04:08,621
So it is coming down.

99
00:04:09,371 --> 00:04:13,864
Speed is the root of seventeen point
three squared plus four point seven

100
00:04:13,864 --> 00:04:14,764
squared.

101
00:04:14,585 --> 00:04:16,816
About eighteen metres per second.

102
00:04:17,466 --> 00:04:18,932
Now, the exam trap.

103
00:04:19,282 --> 00:04:23,478
Many students say that at the highest
point, the acceleration is zero,

104
00:04:23,478 --> 00:04:25,552
because the ball stops going up.

105
00:04:25,952 --> 00:04:27,986
But gravity never switches off.

106
00:04:27,986 --> 00:04:32,413
The acceleration is g, downwards,
at every point, even at the top.

107
00:04:33,063 --> 00:04:34,571
Where is this asked?

108
00:04:34,571 --> 00:04:39,107
In questions on a projectile's position
or velocity at a given time, and

109
00:04:39,107 --> 00:04:40,190
its direction.

110
00:04:40,790 --> 00:04:42,003
Exam level now.

111
00:04:42,003 --> 00:04:46,713
A ball is thrown at thirty metres
per second, at fifty three degrees.

112
00:04:46,713 --> 00:04:50,055
Sine fifty three is point
eight, and g is ten.

113
00:04:50,055 --> 00:04:53,952
When is its velocity perpendicular
to its starting velocity?

114
00:04:53,952 --> 00:04:55,217
Pause and solve.

115
00:05:00,617 --> 00:05:01,956
The answer is B.

116
00:05:01,956 --> 00:05:04,136
Three point seven five seconds.

117
00:05:04,636 --> 00:05:06,437
Split the start velocity.

118
00:05:06,437 --> 00:05:07,803
Across, eighteen.

119
00:05:07,803 --> 00:05:09,180
Up, twenty four.

120
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:12,686
Perpendicular means the
dot product is zero.

121
00:05:12,686 --> 00:05:17,304
Eighteen times eighteen, plus twenty
four times, twenty four minus ten

122
00:05:17,304 --> 00:05:18,436
t, is zero.

123
00:05:18,936 --> 00:05:23,501
So two forty t is nine hundred, and
t is three point seven five seconds.

124
00:05:23,501 --> 00:05:27,135
The flight lasts four point
eight, so it is still flying.

125
00:05:27,735 --> 00:05:29,195
Here is your recap.

126
00:05:29,195 --> 00:05:30,695
Screenshot this card.

127
00:05:33,895 --> 00:05:35,827
Can you answer these without help?

128
00:05:36,226 --> 00:05:37,126
One.

129
00:05:36,705 --> 00:05:39,941
A coin is flicked off a
table, another is dropped.

130
00:05:39,941 --> 00:05:41,817
Which lands first, and why?

131
00:05:42,717 --> 00:05:43,617
Two.

132
00:05:43,184 --> 00:05:46,532
What is the speed of a
projectile at its highest point?

133
00:05:47,432 --> 00:05:48,332
Three.

134
00:05:47,994 --> 00:05:50,787
What is its acceleration
at the highest point?

135
00:05:51,887 --> 00:05:55,795
Next time: why does every
throw make the very same curve?

136
00:05:55,795 --> 00:05:59,176
We find its equation in
trajectory of a projectile.
